  "id": "unconscious-motivation",
  "term": "unconscious motivation",
  "definition": "Unconscious motivation is motivation that operates outside awareness but can still influence behavior and give rise to consciously felt emotions. In the source packet, it is discussed mainly in relation to Freudian drives and brain systems involved in emotion and seeking.",
